Okay, big spoilers coming up...

A quick peruse of the source shows this:

 o If you've got no troubles (or you're highly lucky and on an
   altar - I didn't work out *how* lucky) when you pray, and you're
   piously aligned, then...

 o a random number between 0 and ((luck+6)/2)-1 is rolled.  Depending
   on this (and this is the order in which things are checked) ...

 o 0 : nothing happens;
   1 : your weapon gets uncursed/blessed;
   3 : you get clues about getting into the castle, or if you're already
       in....
   2 : you get surrounded by a golden glow (max hp += 5, cure blindness,
       restore strength (I think), luck gets reset to 0 if less than 0;
   4 : you get surrounded by a light blue aura - all your cursed
       possessions are uncursed;
   5 : you get a gift - telepathy, speed, stealth, or protection, in
       that order.
 7/8 : Yippee!  You've been made the Envoy of Balance, Hand of Elbereth,
       or the Glory of Arioch!  You get an Artifact (or a good sword of
       the same type if the artifact exist)  You also get some intrinsics,
       and your prayer timeout becomes three times greater.
   6 : "An object appears at your feet!"  (it'll be a spellbook)

My apologies if I've got any of this wrong, but that's the way it looks
like it works...

